IMPORT prelude

-- Biological Agents and Toxins Act 2005 (Singapore) -- what a laboratory, importer, courier or facility operator must hold before it
-- may keep, produce, import, transfer or carry a scheduled biological agent or toxin, and what happens if it does not: ss 2
-- ("large-scale production"), 4, 6 to 11, 13 to 18, 20, 22 to 29, 31 to 33, 35, 37, 38 to 39, 44 to 49, 51, 54, 55, 58 and 59.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BATA2005.txt. The deposit's
-- title page says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"; the running footer says "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 9/10/2023", and the latest amendment
-- annotated in the text is S 657/2023 (in force 9 October 2023), with Act 11 of 2023 (in force 1 May 2023) annotated throughout.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0086 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the authorisations an operator, importer, transferor or carrier must hold, the notification
-- deadlines, and the penalty ceilings. Not encoded: the contents of the First to Fifth Schedules (which organisms and toxins fall in
-- which class -- this encoding takes the class as given); ss 5 and 30 (use for a non-peaceful purpose) beyond their penalty and their
-- place in the Eighth Schedule; the Director-General's enforcement powers in ss 52 and 53 beyond the penalty for disobeying an order;
-- s 50's application and revocation machinery beyond s 50(6); the detail of the operator's duties in ss 40 to 44 beyond the fact of
-- them; ss 56, 57 (liability of officers and principals), 60 (appeal), 61, 62 and 63.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Biological Agents and Toxins Act 2005 -- approvals, permits and penalties`

-- The Act does not regulate "biological agents" as one thing: it sorts them into five Schedules and a sixth class (an inactivated
-- First or Second Schedule agent), and nearly every duty and every penalty turns on which class the thing is in. The Fourth Schedule
-- is residual: "Any biological agent that causes death, disease or biological malfunction in a human, other than a First Schedule
-- biological agent or a Second Schedule biological agent."
DECLARE Class IS ONE OF
    `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent`
    `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent`
    `a Second Schedule biological agent`
    `a Third Schedule biological agent`
    `a Fourth Schedule biological agent`
    `an inactivated First or Second Schedule biological agent`
    `a Fifth Schedule toxin`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

§§ `2 -- large-scale production`

-- s 2: "large-scale production", in relation to a biological agent, means "the production by any person of the biological agent using
-- equipment at a facility capable of producing in aggregate 10 or more litres of culture of the biological agent at any one time".
-- The test is the capability of the equipment, not what is actually produced.
GIVEN `litres the equipment can produce at any one time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the production is large-scale` IF
    `litres the equipment can produce at any one time` AT LEAST 10

§§ `4 -- when Parts 3 to 6 do not apply at all`

-- s 4(1): subject to (2) and (3), Parts 3 to 6 -- the whole scheme of approvals, permits, duties and certification -- "with the
-- exception of section 41(e)", do not apply to (a) disposal by a hazardous waste contractor; (b) handling "in the course of carrying
-- out a diagnosis or an autopsy"; (c) collection of food or environmental samples for public-health laboratory analysis; or (d) the
-- use or possession of a finished cosmetic or medicinal product consisting of a toxin, by a lawful manufacturer, supplier, seller or
-- dispenser, by a registered medical practitioner treating a person, or by a person using it for its intended purpose.
-- s 4(2) and (3): despite that, where the thing was provided for an excluded purpose and the person uses, or transfers it to someone
-- who uses it, for another purpose, the Act applies again to that possession, use, transfer and transportation.
-- Even inside an excluded purpose, s 41(e) still binds: nothing may be discharged into the environment without decontamination.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `disposal by a hazardous waste contractor`
    `handling in the course of a diagnosis or an autopsy`
    `collecting food or environmental samples for public health analysis`
    `using a finished cosmetic or medicinal product as intended`
    `research at a laboratory`
    `teaching at a laboratory`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is an excluded purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `disposal by a hazardous waste contractor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `handling in the course of a diagnosis or an autopsy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `collecting food or environmental samples for public health analysis` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `using a finished cosmetic or medicinal product as intended` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `provided for an excluded purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 3 to 6 apply` IF
        (NOT `the purpose is an excluded purpose` `the purpose`)
    OR  (NOT `provided for an excluded purpose`)

§§ `6, 15, 31 -- which classes may not be possessed without an approval`

-- s 6(1) (First Schedule), s 15(1) (Second Schedule) and s 31(1) (Fifth Schedule toxins): a person "must not possess" the thing
-- unless the possession "is authorised by and is in accordance with the conditions of an approval granted by the Director-General".
-- There is no corresponding prohibition on possessing a Third Schedule or Fourth Schedule agent, or an inactivated First or Second
-- Schedule agent: for those classes the Act reaches only production, import and the means of transport.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession requires an approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(2): no approval to possess a First Schedule agent may be granted unless (a) the person is the operator of a certified facility
-- and (b) where it is a Part 2 agent, the facility "is a protected place" (declared under the Infrastructure Protection Act 2017).
-- s 6(3): despite (2)(a), the Director-General MAY grant it to the operator of an uncertified facility if satisfied the activity "will
-- be carried out at such facility in a safe and proper manner" -- so certification is waivable for a First Schedule agent, but the
-- protected-place requirement for a Part 2 agent is not.
-- s 15(2): for a Second Schedule agent the facility must be BOTH a certified facility AND a protected place, and the person must
-- already hold a special approval to handle it under s 14.
-- s 31(2): for a Fifth Schedule toxin the person must be "the operator of a facility which is a protected place" -- a protected place
-- but, on the words of the subsection, not a certified facility.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `operator of a certified facility` IS A BOOLEAN, `the facility is a protected place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director-General is satisfied it will be safe and proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a special approval under section 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an approval to possess may be granted` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN
            `operator of a certified facility`
        OR  `the Director-General is satisfied it will be safe and proper`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN
            `the facility is a protected place`
        AND (   `operator of a certified facility`
             OR `the Director-General is satisfied it will be safe and proper`)
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN
            `operator of a certified facility`
        AND `the facility is a protected place`
        AND `holds a special approval under section 14`
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN `the facility is a protected place`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(4), 15(3), 31(3): the holder "must keep or use" the thing only at the facility specified in the approval to possess.
-- s 6(5), 15(4), 31(4)(a): possessing without an approval, or keeping or using it elsewhere, is the offence.
-- s 6(8), 14(4), 15(7), 31(6): the possession offences do not apply to a person engaged to TRANSPORT the thing within Singapore, or
-- engaged to STORE it pending delivery to the importer or pending export in the course of transhipment, "whose possession ... is
-- merely incidental" to that engagement. A courier or a bonded warehouse therefore needs no approval to possess.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN, `kept at the facility specified in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `engaged only to transport or store it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession is an offence` IF
        `possession requires an approval` `the class`
    AND (NOT `engaged only to transport or store it`)
    AND (   (NOT `holds an approval to possess`)
         OR (NOT `kept at the facility specified in the approval`))

§§ `7, 16, 23 -- large-scale production`

-- s 7(1): no large-scale production of a First Schedule agent without an approval, carried out at the facility specified and on its
-- conditions; s 7(2): that approval cannot be granted to a person who does not already hold an approval to possess under s 6.
-- s 16(1): large-scale production of a Second Schedule agent is flatly prohibited -- no approval is available at all.
-- s 23(1): large-scale production of a Third Schedule agent requires an approval, at the specified facility and on its conditions.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `holds an approval to produce on a large scale` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `produced at the facility specified in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the large-scale production is lawful` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN
            `holds an approval to produce on a large scale`
        AND `holds an approval to possess`
        AND `produced at the facility specified in the approval`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN
            `holds an approval to produce on a large scale`
        AND `holds an approval to possess`
        AND `produced at the facility specified in the approval`
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN
            `holds an approval to produce on a large scale`
        AND `produced at the facility specified in the approval`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(3)(a): unapproved large-scale production of a First Schedule agent -- $100,000 or 10 years or both.
-- s 16(2)(a): large-scale production of a Second Schedule agent -- $100,000 or 10 years or both; but s 16(3) makes contravening the
-- Director-General's consequential order punishable by $1 million or LIFE imprisonment, the Act's heaviest penalty, the same as using
-- an agent for a non-peaceful purpose under s 5.
-- s 23 creates NO offence for the production itself: on the words of s 23(2) and (3), unapproved large-scale production of a Third
-- Schedule agent exposes the producer only to the Director-General's order, and the offence ($10,000 or 12 months) is contravening
-- that order.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlawful large-scale production` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `8, 17, 25, 28, 32 -- import and transhipment permits`

-- s 8(1) and (2) (First Schedule), s 17(1) and (2) (Second Schedule), s 25(1) (Fourth Schedule), s 28(1) (inactivated First or Second
-- Schedule) and s 32(1) and (2) (Fifth Schedule toxins): no import, and for all but the Fourth Schedule and inactivated classes no
-- transhipment, without a permit. A Third Schedule agent may be imported without any permit.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `import requires a permit` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 8(3), 17(3), 32(3): a permit to import a First Schedule agent, a Second Schedule agent or a Fifth Schedule toxin "must not be
-- granted to any person unless the person has already been granted an approval to possess" it. No such precondition appears for a
-- Fourth Schedule agent (s 25) or for an inactivated agent (s 28); for the latter the Director-General must instead be satisfied
-- "that the biological agent has been properly inactivated" (s 28(2)).
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director-General is satisfied it was properly inactivated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a permit to import may be granted` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an inactivated First or Second Schedule biological agent` THEN `the Director-General is satisfied it was properly inactivated`
    WHEN `a Fourth Schedule biological agent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `holds an approval to possess`

-- s 8(4), 17(4), 25(2), 32(4): every permit to import or tranship "is valid only in respect of one consignment".
-- s 28(4) is the exception: a permit to import an inactivated agent entitles the holder to import "any number of consignments, as
-- specified in the permit", from the same inactivator using the same method.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permit covers one consignment only` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `an inactivated First or Second Schedule biological agent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Penalties for importing without a permit: s 8(5) -- First Schedule (Part 1) $10,000 or 12 months, (Part 2) $100,000 or 10 years;
-- s 17(5) -- Second Schedule $100,000 or 10 years; s 25(3) -- Fourth Schedule $5,000 or 6 months; s 28(5) -- inactivated $5,000 or
-- 6 months; s 32(5) -- Fifth Schedule toxin $100,000 or 10 years.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for importing without a permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN 0
    WHEN `a Fourth Schedule biological agent` THEN 5000
    WHEN `an inactivated First or Second Schedule biological agent` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN 100000

§§ `9, 18, 33 -- the consignment that does not arrive`

-- s 9(1), 18(1), 33(1): the permit holder "must immediately notify the Director-General" if it fails to receive the consignment.
-- The duty is imposed on the holder of a permit to import a First Schedule (PART 2) agent, a Second Schedule agent or a Fifth
-- Schedule toxin -- not on the importer of a First Schedule (Part 1) agent, a Fourth Schedule agent or an inactivated agent.
-- s 9(2), 18(2), 33(2): failure to receive is DEEMED if the consignment does not arrive "within 24 hours of such time as may be
-- reasonably estimated by the holder of the permit for the receipt".
-- s 9(3), 18(3), 33(3): $10,000, with no imprisonment.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a failed import must be notified` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `hours after the estimated time of receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignment is deemed not received` IF
    `hours after the estimated time of receipt` GREATER THAN 24

§§ `11, 20, 35 -- transfers`

-- s 11(1) (First Schedule), s 20(1) (Second Schedule), s 35(1) (Fifth Schedule toxins): a person must not transfer the thing unless
-- the transferor holds an approval to possess it AND the transferee either holds one too or "is outside Singapore".
-- s 11(3), 20(3), 35(3): the OFFENCE is narrower than the prohibition. It is committed by a transferor who transfers to a transferee
-- in Singapore "knowing or having reason to believe that such transferee does not have an approval to possess". A transferor who
-- himself holds no approval, but whose transferee does, breaches s 11(1) without committing the s 11(3) offence.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `the transferor holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the transferee holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN, `the transferee is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Where possession needs no approval at all (the Third and Fourth Schedule classes, and an inactivated agent) the Act says nothing
-- about transfers, so a transfer of one is unregulated.
DECIDE `the transfer is permitted` IF
        (NOT `possession requires an approval` `the class`)
    OR  (   `the transferor holds an approval to possess`
        AND (   `the transferee holds an approval to possess`
             OR `the transferee is outside Singapore`))

GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `the transferee holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the transferee is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the transferor knew or had reason to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is an offence` IF
        `possession requires an approval` `the class`
    AND (NOT `the transferee is outside Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `the transferee holds an approval to possess`)
    AND `the transferor knew or had reason to believe`

-- s 12(1), 21(1), 36(1): before transferring a First Schedule (Part 2) agent, ANY Second Schedule agent or a Fifth Schedule toxin the
-- transferor must notify the Director-General of the proposed transfer, tell the transferee an estimated time of receipt, and give an
-- independent carrier "a 24-hour emergency number that is monitored at all times" by someone who knows the hazards or has immediate
-- access to someone who does.
-- s 12(2) to (4), 21(2) to (4), 36(2) to (4): the TRANSFEREE must immediately notify the Director-General of a failure of receipt,
-- deemed if the thing does not arrive within 24 hours of the estimated time the transferor gave. $10,000.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a transfer must be notified in advance` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `13, 22, 24, 26, 29, 37 -- mail and public transport`

-- s 13(1), 22(1), 24(1), 26(1), 29(1), 37(1): "A person must not transport or procure the transportation of" the thing "within
-- Singapore by mail or public transportation". Every class is covered, including the residual Fourth Schedule class and an inactivated
-- agent. "Public transportation" is defined in s 2 to include a taxi.
-- Penalties: First Schedule (Part 1) and Third Schedule $10,000 or 12 months; First Schedule (Part 2), Second Schedule and Fifth
-- Schedule toxins $100,000 or 10 years; Fourth Schedule and inactivated agents $5,000 or 6 months.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for sending it by mail or public transport` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a Fourth Schedule biological agent` THEN 5000
    WHEN `an inactivated First or Second Schedule biological agent` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN 100000

§§ `27 -- inactivation`

-- s 27(1): a person must not inactivate a First or Second Schedule agent unless the person holds the approval to possess it and the
-- inactivation is carried out by a method approved by the person's own biosafety committee and at the facility specified in that
-- approval. s 27(2): this does not apply "insofar as the inactivation relates to the decontamination of" First or Second Schedule
-- biological agent waste -- so routine autoclaving of waste is outside the section.
-- s 27(3) and (4): an attempt counts "whether or not the inactivation is successful"; the offence is contravening the consequential
-- order, $5,000 or 6 months.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN, `the method was approved by the biosafety committee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `carried out at the facility specified in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is decontamination of waste` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inactivation is permitted` IF
        `it is decontamination of waste`
    OR  CONSIDER `the class`
        WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN
                `holds an approval to possess`
            AND `the method was approved by the biosafety committee`
            AND `carried out at the facility specified in the approval`
        WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN
                `holds an approval to possess`
            AND `the method was approved by the biosafety committee`
            AND `carried out at the facility specified in the approval`
        WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN
                `holds an approval to possess`
            AND `the method was approved by the biosafety committee`
            AND `carried out at the facility specified in the approval`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `38, 39, 44, 45 -- the operator's duties`

-- s 38(1): the Part 5 Division 1 duties bind the operator of a facility granted an approval to possess a First or Second Schedule
-- agent or a Fifth Schedule toxin, or an approval to produce a First or Third Schedule agent on a large scale. An operator who holds
-- no approval at all -- a Fourth Schedule laboratory, say -- carries none of them.
-- s 39(1): every such operator must appoint a biosafety committee comprising the persons in the Sixth Schedule and a biosafety
-- co-ordinator. s 39(3) and (6): no activity may commence until the committee has advised on the safety measures and determined the
-- activity may be carried out safely, and the co-ordinator has implemented what the committee devised. s 39(7): the committee must
-- review its measures "every 2 years or earlier, as may be appropriate".
-- ss 40 to 44: maintain the facility, control access, display the Seventh Schedule biohazard sign at every door, run pest control,
-- train and protect staff, escort visitors, keep an inventory and a visitor record, and report infections, adverse incidents, losses
-- and destructions of stock immediately.
GIVEN `holds an approval to possess` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds an approval to produce on a large scale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Division 1 duties apply` IF
        `holds an approval to possess`
    OR  `holds an approval to produce on a large scale`

GIVEN `appointed a biosafety committee and a co-ordinator` IS A BOOLEAN, `the committee determined the activity may be carried out safely` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the co-ordinator implemented the committee's measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity may commence` IF
        `appointed a biosafety committee and a co-ordinator`
    AND `the committee determined the activity may be carried out safely`
    AND `the co-ordinator implemented the committee's measures`

-- s 45(1)(a): breach of any Division 1 duty -- $10,000 or 12 months or both, "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further
-- fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- s 45(3): a biosafety committee that advises "in a reckless or grossly negligent manner or in bad faith" -- EVERY member is guilty
-- ($10,000 or 12 months) unless the member proves the advice was given without his consent or connivance and that he exercised all
-- due diligence to prevent it.
-- s 45(4): a member of STAFF who fails to comply with a measure the co-ordinator implemented is personally guilty -- $10,000 or
-- 12 months.
GIVEN `days the offence continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty for a continuing duty breach` MEANS
    10000 PLUS (1000 TIMES `days the offence continued after conviction`)

§§ `46 to 49 -- carriers`

-- s 46(1): the carrier duties bind "any carrier, being a person (including a transferor or transferee) who undertakes the
-- transportation in Singapore of" a First Schedule agent, a Second Schedule agent, "any Third Schedule biological agent in quantities
-- aggregating 10 litres or more carried on any conveyance at any one time", or a Fifth Schedule toxin. A Fourth Schedule agent or an
-- inactivated agent is outside Division 2 altogether, and a Third Schedule agent only enters it at 10 litres.
-- s 47: no unreasonable delays; the driver must be trained in managing accidents involving biohazardous materials; the conveyance
-- must carry the biohazard panel or label the Director-General requires; on any spillage or leakage the driver must "immediately
-- cordon off the area" and "immediately notify the Commissioner of the Singapore Civil Defence Force"; and for the higher classes the
-- carrier must secure the load, "including the use of security personnel".
-- s 48: packing and labelling is the TRANSFEROR's duty, not the carrier's.
-- s 49: contravening any provision of Division 2 -- a flat $10,000, with no imprisonment, whatever the class.
GIVEN `the class` IS A Class, `litres on the conveyance at any one time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier duties apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 1) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a First Schedule (Part 2) biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Second Schedule biological agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Fifth Schedule toxin` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Third Schedule biological agent` THEN `litres on the conveyance at any one time` AT LEAST 10
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `50(6), 51 -- when an authorisation lapses`

-- s 50(6): an approval to possess "ceases to be valid" when the holder ceases to be the operator of the facility specified in it, or
-- when a facility that the Act requires to be certified ceases to be certified. No decision of the Director-General is needed.
-- s 51(2): a certification ceases to be valid on the earlier of "the expiry of one year from the date of the certification" or "any
-- design or structural change made to the facility". A refit therefore ends the certification, and with it (s 50(6)(b)) the approval
-- to possess that depended on it.
-- s 51(4): before storing or working with an agent at a newly certified facility the operator must tell the Director-General and hand
-- over the certification body's report.
GIVEN `months since the certification` IS A NUMBER, `a design or structural change was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certification is still valid` IF
        `months since the certification` AT MOST 12
    AND (NOT `a design or structural change was made`)

GIVEN `still the operator of the facility specified` IS A BOOLEAN, `certification is required for this facility` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since the certification` IS A NUMBER, `a design or structural change was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approval to possess is still valid` IF
        `still the operator of the facility specified`
    AND (   (NOT `certification is required for this facility`)
         OR `the certification is still valid` `months since the certification` `a design or structural change was made`)

§§ `54 -- 48 hours to challenge a seizure`

-- s 54(1)(b): a person aggrieved by a seizure "may, within 48 hours after the seizure, complain thereof to a Magistrate's Court",
-- which may confirm, disallow, order return on conditions, or order reasonable compensation for loss or depreciation.
-- s 54(2): if no complaint reaches the Court within 48 hours, or the Court confirms the seizure, the thing seized "becomes the
-- property of the Government" and is destroyed or disposed of as the Director-General thinks fit.
GIVEN `hours since the seizure` IS A NUMBER, `complained to a Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court confirmed the seizure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized matter becomes Government property` IF
        (   `complained to a Magistrate's Court`
        AND `hours since the seizure` AT MOST 48
        AND `the Court confirmed the seizure`)
    OR  (   `hours since the seizure` GREATER THAN 48
        AND (NOT `complained to a Magistrate's Court`))

§§ `55, 58, 59 -- obstruction, the court, and paying instead`

-- s 55: hindering, obstructing or molesting the Director-General or an enforcement officer -- $5,000 or 6 months for a first offence,
-- $10,000 or 12 months for a second or subsequent one.
-- s 58: a District Court may try any offence under the Act "other than the offences under sections 5, 16 and 30" and impose the full
-- punishment. The three excepted sections are use for a non-peaceful purpose (ss 5 and 30) and large-scale production of a Second
-- Schedule agent (s 16).
-- s 59(1): the Director-General may compound any offence except those in the Eighth Schedule, for "a sum not exceeding the lower of"
-- half the maximum fine and $5,000. The Eighth Schedule names only ss 5 and 30. So large-scale production of a Second Schedule agent,
-- which a District Court may not try, is nonetheless compoundable -- for at most $5,000 against a $100,000 maximum fine.
GIVEN `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstruction` MEANS
    IF `it is a second or subsequent offence` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `it is an offence under section 5 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is compoundable` IF
    NOT `it is an offence under section 5 or 30`

GIVEN `the maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `it is an offence under section 5 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an offence under section 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court may try the offence` IF
        (NOT `it is an offence under section 5 or 30`)
    AND (NOT `it is an offence under section 16`)
